{"sourceSha256": "5eea63391e19d4eda00b72f0302aa954761d97afdb16207514af5e2c2c7c4c72", "text": "SETTING\n\nPATIENT\n\nTASK\n\nOET AUGUST 2015\n\nROLEPLAYER CARD NO. 6 MEDICINE\n\nPrivate Medical Clinic\n\nYou are a 40-year-old office worker and have come to the doctor because you\nfainted on the train yesterday. You feel that you are healthy (though you eat mainly\na vegan diet) and believe that you only fainted because the train was hot and\ncrowded. However, your spouse insisted that you see the doctor.\n\n* Tell the doctor that you were unconscious for only a few seconds when you\nfainted. You experienced no other symptoms,\n\n* Explain that you are very healthy and eat mainly a vegan diet (no dairy or meat).\nYou work very hard but find time to exercise every day (e.g,, walking for one\nhour, etc.).\n\n* Answer the doctor's questions: you often feel tired and irritable, and occasionally\nsuffer from diarrhoea but have no other symptoms.\n\n* Refuse to accept the doctor's diagnosis of malnutrition. Remind tae doctor that\nyou eat mainly fresh frult and vegetables,\n\n* Reluctantly agree to blood tests.\ne Agree to increase the protein in your diet and return for a review in two weeks.\n\n‘© Cambridge Boxhill Language Assessment AUGUST 2015\n\n69\n\nOET AUGUST 2015\nCANDIDATE CARD NO. 6 MEDICINE\n\nSETTING\n\nDOCTOR\n\nTASK\n\nPrivate Medical Clinic\n\nYou are speaking to a 40-year-old office worker who fainted on the train yesterday.\nThe patient thinks that he/she fainted because the train was hot and crowded but\nthe patient's spouse insisted that he/she come to see you. The patient eats mainly\na vegan diet (no dairy or meat). You suspect arrhythmia, which is a common\nsymptom of malnutrition where there may be an electrolyte imbalance.\n\n¢ Ask the patient to explain what happened when he/she fainted.\n\n* Ask about his/her lifestyle (e.g., dict, work, exercise, etc.)\n\n* Ask about other symptoms (e.g., fatigue, irritability, diarrhoea, palpitations,\ntongue biting, loss of bowel and bladder control, etc.).\n\n* Explain your suspected diagnosis (arhythmia, malnutrition) to the patient.\n\n* Persuade the patient to take blood tests to exclude iron deficiency anaemia and\nto check that other electrolytes are within normal limits.\n\n* Encourage the patient to increase protein in his/her diet (e.g., meat, tofu, nuts,\netc.) and return for a review in two weeks.", "pages": [{"number": 1, "text": "SETTING\n\nPATIENT\n\nTASK\n\nOET AUGUST 2015\n\nROLEPLAYER CARD NO. 6 MEDICINE\n\nPrivate Medical Clinic\n\nYou are a 40-year-old office worker and have come to the doctor because you\nfainted on the train yesterday. You feel that you are healthy (though you eat mainly\na vegan diet) and believe that you only fainted because the train was hot and\ncrowded. However, your spouse insisted that you see the doctor.\n\n* Tell the doctor that you were unconscious for only a few seconds when you\nfainted. You experienced no other symptoms,\n\n* Explain that you are very healthy and eat mainly a vegan diet (no dairy or meat).\nYou work very hard but find time to exercise every day (e.g,, walking for one\nhour, etc.).\n\n* Answer the doctor's questions: you often feel tired and irritable, and occasionally\nsuffer from diarrhoea but have no other symptoms.\n\n* Refuse to accept the doctor's diagnosis of malnutrition. Remind tae doctor that\nyou eat mainly fresh frult and vegetables,\n\n* Reluctantly agree to blood tests.\ne Agree to increase the protein in your diet and return for a review in two weeks.\n\n‘© Cambridge Boxhill Language Assessment AUGUST 2015\n\n69\n\nOET AUGUST 2015\nCANDIDATE CARD NO. 6 MEDICINE\n\nSETTING\n\nDOCTOR\n\nTASK\n\nPrivate Medical Clinic\n\nYou are speaking to a 40-year-old office worker who fainted on the train yesterday.\nThe patient thinks that he/she fainted because the train was hot and crowded but\nthe patient's spouse insisted that he/she come to see you. The patient eats mainly\na vegan diet (no dairy or meat). You suspect arrhythmia, which is a common\nsymptom of malnutrition where there may be an electrolyte imbalance.\n\n¢ Ask the patient to explain what happened when he/she fainted.\n\n* Ask about his/her lifestyle (e.g., dict, work, exercise, etc.)\n\n* Ask about other symptoms (e.g., fatigue, irritability, diarrhoea, palpitations,\ntongue biting, loss of bowel and bladder control, etc.).\n\n* Explain your suspected diagnosis (arhythmia, malnutrition) to the patient.\n\n* Persuade the patient to take blood tests to exclude iron deficiency anaemia and\nto check that other electrolytes are within normal limits.\n\n* Encourage the patient to increase protein in his/her diet (e.g., meat, tofu, nuts,\netc.) and return for a review in two weeks.", "extraction": "ocr", "layout": {"version": 1, "width": 1979.0, "height": 2800.0, "blocks": [{"text": "SETTING", "lines": [{"text": "SETTING", "x": 0.04194, "y": 0.10071, "width": 0.07832, "height": 0.01071, "confidence": 0.962, "words": [{"text": "SETTING", "x": 0.04194, "width": 0.07832, "confidence": 0.962}], "uncertainWords": []}]}, {"text": "PATIENT", "lines": [{"text": "PATIENT", "x": 0.04396, "y": 0.13357, "width": 0.08287, "height": 0.01071, "confidence": 0.96, "words": [{"text": "PATIENT", "x": 0.04396, "width": 0.08287, "confidence": 0.96}], "uncertainWords": []}]}, {"text": "TASK", "lines": [{"text": "TASK", "x": 0.04093, "y": 0.26857, "width": 0.04851, "height": 0.01143, "confidence": 0.955, "words": [{"text": "TASK", "x": 0.04093, "width": 0.04851, "confidence": 0.955}], "uncertainWords": []}]}, {"text": "OET AUGUST 2015", "lines": [{"text": "OET AUGUST 2015", "x": 0.4098, "y": 0.04286, "width": 0.21223, "height": 0.01429, "confidence": 0.947, "words": [{"text": "OET", "x": 0.4098, "width": 0.0475, "confidence": 0.909}, {"text": "AUGUST", "x": 0.46286, "width": 0.09904, "confidence": 0.962}, {"text": "2015", "x": 0.56847, "width": 0.05356, "confidence": 0.968}], "uncertainWords": []}]}, {"text": "ROLEPLAYER CARD